[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

; A berry plot. GAME_DESIGN.md 21: "Plant -> wait -> harvest. No watering
; chores."
;
; PART STAND-IN, PART REAL. The soil bed and its timber rim are primitive
; geometry at honest dimensions (1.70 x 1.70m, 0.14m deep, one 2m build cell).
; The plants are the meadow's own `Bush_Common` and `Bush_Common_Flowers` from
; the Quaternius Stylized Nature MegaKit, scaled down — so a cultivated berry
; bush is visibly the same plant as the wild ones the player has been foraging
; from, which is most of what makes farming read as farming.
;
; THE THREE GROWTH STAGES ARE THE POINT OF THIS FILE. `Seedling`, `Growing` and
; `Ripe` are three sibling nodes and the BerryPlot station in
; scripts/building/station.gd shows exactly one of them, the same way the
; campfire's Hearth shows and hides `Flame`. That is what makes a half-grown plot
; visibly half-grown, including after a reload. If these nodes are renamed,
; rename them in data/building/pieces.json too — the definition names them there
; rather than the code hard-coding a path into a scene.

[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/environment/stylized_nature/Bush_Common.gltf" id="bush"]

[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/environment/stylized_nature/Bush_Common_Flowers.gltf" id="berry_bush"]

